{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/REST Architectural Style.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/REST Architectural Style.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"rest architectural style rest architectural style","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/REST Architectural Style.md","fileName":"REST Architectural Style.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"REST Architectural Style","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 10:58\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[REST Architectural Constraints and Hypermedia]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["REST Architectural Constraints and Hypermedia","hands-onrestfulwebserviceswithaspnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/REST Architectural Style.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/REST Architectural Style.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"rest architectural style rest architectural style","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/REST Architectural Style.md","fileName":"REST Architectural Style.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"REST Architectural Style","heading":"REST Architectural Style","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Representational State Transfer is an architectural style for networked systems built from constraints rather than a prescribed wire format. It organizes an API around resources, representations, self-descriptive messages, stateless exchanges, cacheability, client-server separation, and layered intermediaries.\n\nCompliance is a system property rather than a label attached to JSON over HTTP. Each constraint changes how clients and servers evolve, scale, and understand an interaction, so adopting only an HTTP endpoint does not by itself make a service RESTful.","tags":["baby"],"links":["REST Architectural Constraints and Hypermedia","hands-onrestfulwebserviceswithaspnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/REST Architectural Style.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/REST Architectural Style.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"rest architectural style rest architectural style","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/REST Architectural Style.md","fileName":"REST Architectural Style.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"REST Architectural Style","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[hands-onrestfulwebserviceswithaspnetcore3.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["REST Architectural Constraints and Hypermedia","hands-onrestfulwebserviceswithaspnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}